{"ts":"2026-07-26T18:28:20.913Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"a31af454c29fc92c25cebfd4","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Problem\n\npm-a22j (closed) built scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs: it measures the\nfull agent-facing token surface — root help, every per-command help, the\ncontracts payload family, and the MCP tools/list payload — and emits JSON so a\nratchet can diff it. pm-ksca (closed) then added a covering spec for it.\n\nThe harness is wired into nothing. Repository-wide search for\n`measure-agent-token-surface` outside the script itself returns exactly one\nhit, a historical CHANGELOG line. It has no package.json script, no CI step,\nand no recorded baseline to diff against. Its own header comment tells the\nreader to \"re-run after each consolidation slice lands and diff against the\nrecorded baseline\" — a baseline that is not stored anywhere in the repo.\n\n## Consequence, measured 2026-07-26 on the live workspace\n\nNothing detects token-surface regressions, and they are present:\n\n| command | output | approx tokens |\n|---|---|---|\n| pm graph audit --summary | 1,534 B | ~383 |\n| pm list-open --limit 20 | 4,556 B | ~1,139 |\n| pm get pm-96h7 | 5,365 B | ~1,341 |\n| pm context --limit 10 | 6,195 B | ~1,548 |\n| pm next --limit 5 | 8,799 B | ~2,199 |\n| pm validate | 22,719 B | ~5,679 |\n| **pm health --check-only** | **132,585 B** | **~33,146** |\n\n`pm health --check-only` is the diagnostic AGENTS.md \"When Unsure\" routes\nagents to, and a single invocation costs roughly a sixth of a 200k context\nwindow. That specific regression is owned by pm-du93sr and `graph impact` by\npm-mfy1ux — this item owns the reason such regressions land and persist\nundetected: the instrument that would have caught them on the commit that\nintroduced them runs nowhere.\n\n## Why this is a child of pm-5t33or, not a duplicate\n\npm-5t33or owns the forward design: every command declares a default output\nceiling in its contract and degrades deterministically when it would exceed it.\nThat is the destination. This item is the enabling tranche that can ship\nindependently and immediately: take the harness that already exists and already\nhas a spec, record a committed baseline, and fail CI when the surface grows\nbeyond it. It requires no contract changes and no command behaviour changes,\nand it makes pm-5t33or's rollout measurable slice by slice instead of\nretrospective.\n\n## Direction (not a mandate for the fix)\n\nAdd a package.json script, commit a baseline JSON artifact next to the\nsdk-surface-snapshot baseline that already follows this pattern, and add a\nstatic CI gate that diffs current against baseline with an allowed-growth\nthreshold and a documented update path. The sdk-surface-snapshot gate is the\nworking precedent for exactly this shape."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-dpqa3h"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The agent token-surface harness from pm-a22j is wired into nothing, so output-size regressions like the 33k-token health check land undetected"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs measures root help, per-command help, contracts payloads and MCP tools/list, and has a covering spec, but has no package.json script, no CI step and no committed baseline. Repo-wide search finds one reference outside the file itself, a historical CHANGELOG line."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","ci-gate","observability","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-26T18:28:20.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T18:28:20.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A package.json script runs the token-surface harness and a committed baseline artifact records the current surface; A static CI gate diffs measured against baseline and fails when growth exceeds the declared threshold, with a documented baseline-update path; The gate reproduces the currently measured values for health, validate, context, next, get and list-open so the baseline is verifiable"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Turns an already-built, already-tested measurement into a continuous ratchet, so token regressions are caught at authoring time instead of during a manual audit."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Every agent-facing payload can grow without limit today; token cost is the scarcest resource in the agent loop."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"A committed token-surface baseline plus a static CI gate that fails on growth beyond a declared threshold, following the sdk-surface-snapshot precedent."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"pm health --check-only currently emits 132,585 B (~33k tokens) and is the diagnostic AGENTS.md routes agents to; the instrument that would have flagged it on the introducing commit exists and runs nowhere."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0556c17a376f4a1c4ef8799e3602f0a8698f80150367cc1694d59a8656123e1f","message":""}
